    {
      "id": "s02",
      "type": "TITLE_CARD",
      "transition": "fade",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Welcome back. Apple's finally made a folding iPhone, and it's called the Duo. Today we're going through what actually unfolds, what it costs, and the one design decision nobody else has managed. So is a two thousand dollar iPhone a real product, or a statement?",
      "data": {
        "title": "What folding actually buys you",
        "subtitle": "iPhone Duo, in numbers",
        "atWord": 14.583
      },
      "durationFrames": 447,
      "audio": "audio/duo_long_s02.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s03",
      "type": "APPLE_STAGE",
      "transition": "wipe",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Start with the geometry, because that decides whether a fold is useful or a gimmick. Closed, the Duo's eighty four millimetres across. Open it and the width doubles to one sixty five, while the height never moves. So it doesn't become a taller phone. It becomes a wider one.",
      "data": {
        "appleStage": {
          "headline": "The width [doubles]. The height does not.",
          "kind": "duo-pair",
          "caption": "84.1 mm closed, 164.6 mm open",
          "premise": "Both states drawn to the same scale, from the published dimensions.",
          "color": "purple",
          "cells": [
            {
              "label": "Closed",
              "text": "outer",
              "sub": "84.1 mm across",
              "atWord": 13.25
            },
            {
              "label": "Open",
              "text": "inner",
              "sub": "164.6 mm across",
              "atWord": 21.833
            },
            {
              "label": "The hinge",
              "text": "hinge",
              "sub": "down the centre",
              "atWord": 23.583
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 521,
      "audio": "audio/duo_long_s03.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s04",
      "type": "RECORDED_STEP",
      "transition": "letterbox",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Apple leads on exactly that. Its own page calls this the largest iPhone display ever, in a thin foldable design, and those two halves are the whole product: a screen that would never fit a pocket, folded until it does.",
